{:goal "Show that the derivative-style bounded slope condition is equivalent to uniform continuity on (0,1)."
 :terms [{:name "uniform continuity"
          :meaning "∀ε>0 ∃δ>0 so that |x-y|<δ ⇒ |f(x)-f(y)|<ε."
          :needed-because "One direction uses uniform continuity directly; the other uses its negation."
         }
         {:name "slope threshold N"
          :meaning "Choose N so large that if |(f(x)-f(y))/(x-y)| exceeds N then |x-y| must be smaller than the δ supplied by uniform continuity."
          :needed-because "Translating uniform continuity constants into the given (b) statement is the crux of (a) ⇒ (b)."
         }
         {:name "contrapositive via sequences"
          :meaning "If uniform continuity fails, pick sequences with |x_n - y_n|→0 but |f(x_n)-f(y_n)|≥ε₀; their slopes diverge."
          :needed-because "This shows (b) ⇒ (a) by contradiction."}]
